  "passage": "Tina wanted to try a new restaurant because it had hundreds of five-star reviews online. Her brother noticed something odd. Many reviews used almost the same words and were posted on the same day.\nThey checked other sites and found more mixed opinions. Some customers liked the restaurant, but many complained about slow service.\nTina still went, but she no longer expected perfection. The food was good, and the service was indeed slow.\nShe learned that reviews are useful, but they are not pure truth. Numbers can be shaped, bought, or repeated.\nA smart reader does not only count stars. A smart reader asks who wrote them, when, and why.",
